 any admin-added iptables/ip6tables rule was silently lost. Ordering against
 pnet-fwd-reconcile.sh's own PNETLAB-FWD chain matters: see the drop-in at
 engine-custom/etc/systemd/system/pnetlab-ovfstartup.service.d/ and the
 comment above reconcile_iptables() in pnet-fwd-reconcile.sh. Installer/
 upgrade apt-get calls already run with DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive, so
 the package's debconf autosave question is answered from its own default,
 no explicit preseed needed. ebtables/L2 persistence is explicitly OUT OF
 SCOPE -- PNETLAB-L2 is reconciled fresh every boot by design, never
 admin-customizable; see D1 in docs/pass2-design/03-revised-plan.md.
